 In Rust, you can define the `is_even` function more concisely using pattern matching instead of multiple `if-else if` statements. Here's how you can transform the given JavaScript code into Rust:

```rust
fn is_even(n: i32) -> bool {
 match n {
     0 => true,
     1 | 3 | 5 | 7 | 9 => false,
     _ => {
         if n % 2 == 0 {
             true
         } else {
             false
         }
     },
 }
}
