 To prevent the planets from being generated too close to each other, you can modify the `generateRandomPlanets` function by implementing a rejection mechanism when placing a new planet if it's too close to any existing one. Here's an updated version of your function:

```typescript
const generateRandomPlanets = (numPlanets, minDistance) => {
  const planets = []
  let attempts = 0

  while (planets.length < numPlanets && attempts < 100) {
    attempts++

    const planet = {
      position: [
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
      ],
      size: randomSize(1, 5) * scale,
      color: randomColor(),
      ringSize: 0.2 * scale,
      ringColor: randomColor(),
      ringNoise: 0.3 * scale,
    }

    let isTooClose = false

    for (let i = 0; i < planets.length; i++) {
      const existingPlanet = planets[i]
      for (let j = 0; j < 3; j++) {
        const distance = Math.abs(planet.position[j] - existingPlanet.position[j]);
        if (distance < minDistance) {
          isTooClose = true
          break
        }
      }

      if (!isTooClose) {
        planets.push(planet)
        break
      }
    }

    if (!isTooClose) {
      break
    }
  }

  return planets
}
```

This implementation checks for collisions between the new planet and all existing ones, and only adds it to the list if there's no collision detected. This way, the planets will be generated at a minimum distance from each other, ensuring a better distribution in your scene.

 I'm here to help you write a React utility function to remove widows in your text. Widows are the last line of a paragraph that is left-aligned and has only one word or a few short words, which can look visually unappealing. Here's a simple utility function that you can use in your React project:

```javascript
import PropTypes from 'prop-types';

const WIDOWS_THRESHOLD = 3; // Number of characters below the line for a widow

function preventWidows(text, lineHeight) {
  const lines = text.split('\n');
  const lastLineIndex = lines.length - 1;
  const lastLine = lines[lastLineIndex];

  if (lastLine.length <= WIDOWS_THRESHOLD && lastLineIndex !== 0) {
    const penultimateLine = lines[lastLineIndex - 1];
    const combinedLines = `${penultimateLine} ${lastLine}`;
    const linesWithCombinedLastLines = lines.slice(0, lastLineIndex).concat([combinedLines]);
    return linesWithCombinedLastLines.join('\n');
  }

  return text;
}

const PreventWidows = ({ children, style }) => {
  const formattedText = preventWidows(children.toString(), style.lineHeight);

  return <p style={style}>{formattedText}</p>;
};

PreventWidows.propTypes = {
  children: PropTypes.node.isRequired,
  style: PropTypes.shape({
    lineHeight: PropTypes.number.isRequired,
  }).isRequired,
};

export default PreventWidows;
```

